    "abstract": "We examine the relationship between retail investors’ trading activity and herding behaviour in the Korean equity market, where retail participation has increased substantially. Using 30 years of market data, we find that the growth in the number of retail investors and their trading volumes significantly amplifies herding behaviour. While short-term herding is observed under all market conditions, long-term herding primarily emerges during market downturns, driven by psychological biases such as excessive risk aversion and fear of missing out (FOMO).",
